    No source code from CMDV is copied into this project. CMDV is written in
    Kotlin against a different data model; every file here is an independent
    implementation in Java.

    Two ideas in CMDV's resource listener did inform the design of this
    project's scanner, and are acknowledged as its contribution:

      1. Carrying a "has this branch passed through custom model data" flag
         down the recursion over an item definition's model tree, and treating
         only the models reached that way as belonging to the pack. This is the
         reachability test that separates a pack's own models from the
         thousands of vanilla ones, and it is the right test.

      2. Accumulating the select-case values and range-dispatch thresholds
         along the route so that the component needed to reproduce a model on a
         real item can be rebuilt from them.

    Both are reimplemented here, extended to Minecraft 26.2's full node set,
    and corrected in two places where CMDV's version loses information: a
    "when" clause holding an array of values (which vanilla's own trident.json
    uses), and the fallback branch of a custom model data selection, which
    means the opposite of having been selected by one.

    See dev/custommodels/cmv/explorer/def/ItemDefinitionParser.java and
    dev/custommodels/cmv/explorer/graph/GraphBuilder.java, where these
    acknowledgements are repeated at the point of use.

